# Helsinki UDBMS Film: an IMDb document dump against two independently built graphs.
#
# There is no relational side; the publisher ships none. What this instance carries that Patent and
# Person do not is a correspondence that a comparison relation improves and does not repair. A film
# title normalises onto a graph subject the way a person's page title does -- spaces to underscores,
# case folded -- but where Person reaches 0.999967 this reaches 0.419 against DBpedia and 0.194
# against YAGO. The residue is not a threshold away: the dump holds duplicate and conflicting
# records for one film, and a title identifies a film only loosely.
#
# Two graphs rather than one, because they disagree. DBpedia and YAGO name the same films by
# different conventions, so the instance shows the same document side reaching two graphs at
# different degrees -- a property of the graphs rather than of the method.

mongo        mongo  hfilm  films

neo4j-label  graph  neo4j  FilmDBpedia
neo4j-label  graph  neo4j  FilmYago

neo4j-rels   graph  neo4j  DBPEDIA
neo4j-rels   graph  neo4j  YAGO
